{
  "Motif": "dwarves",
  "Name": "Dwarves",
  "Draw": "Dwarves are short and nearly as wide as they are tall, with thick forearms, heavy brows, and a beard that is the biggest thing about them - braided, ringed, and running down out of the picture. Everything they wear is made rather than found: riveted plate, mail, leather aprons, tools slung and clipped along belts, and metalwork that is clean, deliberate and worn from use. They plant themselves and do not lean.",
  "ElementDraw": {
    "fire": "Forge heat. The beard singed back and full of soot, black in every crease of the skin, the iron glowing dull orange at its working end and sparks standing in the air around it.",
    "ice": "Rime along the mail rings and down the beard braids, breath fogging heavily, the leather gone stiff and white. The skin is chapped and ruddy under cold blue light.",
    "lightning": "Arcs crawl the rivets and run the mail, the beard and hair lift out of their braids, and every tool on the belt is pitted and haloed yellow.",
    "earth": "Rock dust over everything, green stone grit packed into the beard, raw ore set into the plate and grown through the leather. The knuckles have gone to stone.",
    "arcane": "Violet runework burning along the metal and through the beard rings, and light coming out from under the helm rim and the brow with no source in the picture."
  },
  "ValidFloors": [
    2,
    7
  ],
